; `… run return run <command>` with a command the parser does not know (Vanilla Tweaks Graves: `return run rotate`,
; `return run ride`) made the whole line an unparsed fallback that contains a `return`, so the whole function fell
; back to vanilla. Only the unknown command runs through vanilla now; the execute chain and the return stay compiled.
@setup
objective create t dummy

@function f
execute if score #go t matches 1 run return run bossbar set mcfc-test:nested max 7
return 1

@function run
bossbar add mcfc-test:nested "n"
scoreboard players set #go t 1
execute store result score r t run function mcfc-test:f
scoreboard players set #go t 0
execute store result score r0 t run function mcfc-test:f
execute store result score m t run bossbar get mcfc-test:nested max
bossbar remove mcfc-test:nested

@validate
score r t is 7
score r0 t is 1
score m t is 7
